#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166498 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "387be734-719f-52cd-8079-50c744ecdd5e" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Poisson CDF Table"}] :question/id #uuid "d8c1a664-c40a-5525-b1c0-2f977c01077a" :question/math-academy-id "e-15057" :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\textrm{Po}(9).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing value in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.1157\\,$ | $\\,0.2068\\,$ | $\\,0.3239\\,$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,?\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$ | $\\,0.5874\\,$ | $\\,0.7060\\,$ | $\\,0.8030\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\textrm{Po}(\\lambda)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{\\lambda^x e^{-\\lambda}}{x!}, \\qquad x=0,1,2,3, \\ldots\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda=9.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8) & =P(X\\le 8) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 7)+P(X=8) \\\\  & =F(7)+P(X=8) \\\\  & =0.3239+\\frac{{9}^{8}\\cdot {e}^{-9}}{8!} \\\\  & ≈0.4557\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166499 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166736 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "240ed915-56cd-5e22-8c7f-a36ebea90279" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Using a CDF Table"}] :question/id #uuid "a4d766f8-8e20-52a0-afa1-0eea74e6688e" :question/math-academy-id "e-15058" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X \\sim \\textrm{Po}(6)$ given below, compute $P(X=7).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0620\\,$ | $\\,0.1512\\,$ | $\\,0.2851\\,$ | $\\,0.4457\\,$ | $\\,0.6063\\,$ | $\\,0.7440\\,$ | $\\,0.8472\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\})+P(X=7) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6)+P(X=7) \\\\  & =F(6)+P(X=7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=7) & =F(7)-F(6) \\\\  & =0.7440-0.6063 \\\\  & =0.1377.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166500 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166737 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e597d4c-f86f-509e-9fc8-7dd7c03125a1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF Table"}] :question/id #uuid "b73faba8-1021-5d9c-94f5-5e1b908397b0" :question/math-academy-id "e-15059" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X \\sim \\textrm{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(3 \\leq X \\leq 6).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0138\\,$ | $\\,0.0424\\,$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(3\\le X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(3\\le X\\le 6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 6) & =F(6)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.3134-0.0138 \\\\  & =0.2996.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166501 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166738 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e822ac5d-67a0-57b5-b5fe-d3ad03cd91fe" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Containing a \"Greater Than\" Symbol"}] :question/id #uuid "7fb51db3-deb3-5c76-985f-3e43b7cfe995" :question/math-academy-id "e-15060" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X \\sim \\textrm{Po}(7)$ given below, compute $P(X \\geq 5).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0009\\,$ | $\\,0.0073\\,$ | $\\,0.0296\\,$ | $\\,0.0818\\,$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X > a) = 1 - P(X\\leq a) = 1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 5) = P(X \\gt 4).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5) & =P(X>4) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-F(4) \\\\  & =1-0.1730 \\\\  & =0.8270.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "387be734-719f-52cd-8079-50c744ecdd5e" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Poisson CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06a0bcc3-d25c-57e6-b83c-d86187510afa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0067" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06a0bcc3-d25c-57e6-b83c-d86187510afa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0067" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487579} :answer-field/id #uuid "135a22aa-687a-58ad-b9c8-3cd5920b208e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163952} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c67ea15-0a12-572c-9654-5f17c706ecfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0404" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c67ea15-0a12-572c-9654-5f17c706ecfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0404" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487624} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f44ede2-84e8-5397-a08d-0da3d500e3dd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b11a681e-5f0b-530a-8558-f3ac265e8a1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-224475" :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(5).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing values in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.1247\\,$ | $\\,0.2650\\,$ | $\\,0.4405\\,$ | $\\,0.6160\\,$ | $\\,0.7622\\,$ |" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =5.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{0}{e}^{-5}}{0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-5}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0067.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{0}\\cdot {e}^{-5}}{0!}+\\frac{{5}^{1}\\cdot {e}^{-5}}{1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-5}}{1}+\\frac{5\\cdot {e}^{-5}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0404.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "387be734-719f-52cd-8079-50c744ecdd5e" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Poisson CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3202583d-4b37-5bc6-9d6b-3f1926089c3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8305" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3202583d-4b37-5bc6-9d6b-3f1926089c3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8305" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487662} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f6faa2a-0dc2-5f30-b841-93aa87087ebf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93891b8f-eb70-5b7b-b9db-5fefe5271f29" :question/math-academy-id "q-224476" :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(7).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing value in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ | $\\,0.5987\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $\\,0.9015\\,$ |" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =7.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(9) & =P(X\\le 9) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 8)+P(X=9) \\\\  & =F(8)+P(X=9) \\\\  & =0.7291+\\frac{{7}^{9}\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{9!} \\\\  & ≈0.8305.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166736 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "240ed915-56cd-5e22-8c7f-a36ebea90279" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Using a CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2025cdb9-701f-5a0e-a302-0d874be139c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7622" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2025cdb9-701f-5a0e-a302-0d874be139c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7622" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487635} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0ad2e45-8e1f-5af6-a95f-ef60390de509" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ce214f19-3d2c-5b40-b32f-c7c35f404968" :question/math-academy-id "q-224479" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5)$ given below, find the value of $P(X\\le 6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1247\\,$ | $\\,0.2650\\,$ | $\\,0.4405\\,$ | $\\,0.6160\\,$ | $\\,0.7622\\,$ | $\\,0.8666\\,$ | $\\,0.9319\\,$ |\n\n$P(X\\le 6)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 6) & =F(6) \\\\  & =0.7622.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166736 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "240ed915-56cd-5e22-8c7f-a36ebea90279" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Using a CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "724641d5-f288-51a5-8b41-9841bd8281cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0996" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487797} {:answer/id #uuid "7dcf728f-a47d-5e95-aed1-0b2772b763e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0916" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487810} {:answer/id #uuid "8092ef73-0575-5ffe-914c-404ebb71f54a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0845" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487814} {:answer/id #uuid "9862d14e-fa7e-5fe8-862b-20d65e72510b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3134" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487854} {:answer/id #uuid "a9976404-9788-5cfd-942d-efed478db702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1222" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dcf728f-a47d-5e95-aed1-0b2772b763e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0916" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487810} :answer-field/id #uuid "696faedc-2423-51c5-9692-5e7bf27716e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "88a38ed6-7fa9-5b5b-87c9-ffc4db1074d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-224482" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(X=5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0424\\,$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ | $\\,0.7166\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,4\\})+P(X=5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =F(5)-F(4) \\\\  & =0.1912-0.0996 \\\\  & =0.0916.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166738 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e822ac5d-67a0-57b5-b5fe-d3ad03cd91fe" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Containing a \"Greater Than\" Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e082048e-8dd4-5d2c-b2fe-ab849cb511c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7622" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163975} {:answer/id #uuid "447c2395-a77d-5d6a-bb4a-d41a76e2d84b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3561" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163976} {:answer/id #uuid "5199ef22-dfeb-574f-8040-aeba8a14f8a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163977} {:answer/id #uuid "5414da15-f7b3-500f-b0ad-6706e9ba902d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5595" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163978} {:answer/id #uuid "737524cb-a1cf-5346-bbf4-ee57192aebbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3840" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5414da15-f7b3-500f-b0ad-6706e9ba902d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5595" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163978} :answer-field/id #uuid "baa3313c-d7b1-5971-8c53-5efce0147dba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a804742-ead0-5d3f-8196-ee5a543e15d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-224490" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5)$ given below, compute $P(X>4).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1247\\,$ | $\\,0.2650\\,$ | $\\,0.4405\\,$ | $\\,0.6160\\,$ | $\\,0.7622\\,$ | $\\,0.8666\\,$ | $\\,0.9319\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-F(4) \\\\  & =1-0.4405 \\\\  & =0.5595.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166738 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e822ac5d-67a0-57b5-b5fe-d3ad03cd91fe" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Containing a \"Greater Than\" Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae507cd0-e5ef-5c7c-b901-a53e3652dcf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0166" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163981} {:answer/id #uuid "af12340b-9c97-5945-95ed-2ee844d17f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1606" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163982} {:answer/id #uuid "d285675c-9ccd-551f-87a2-bd09d0a3f0a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9473" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163983} {:answer/id #uuid "f17ceaf4-752d-5836-ac4e-a7583891de19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0527" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163984} {:answer/id #uuid "04152e8f-6915-5e4c-a6ad-604bca00597c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1429" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04152e8f-6915-5e4c-a6ad-604bca00597c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1429" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163985} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd90ac7b-1336-5a42-ab85-e796b0262a6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "31265a8f-4b43-5628-ae12-6c047eef09ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-224491" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(2)$ given below, compute $P(X\\ge 4).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.6767\\,$ | $\\,0.8571\\,$ | $\\,0.9473\\,$ | $\\,0.9834\\,$ | $\\,0.9955\\,$ | $\\,0.9989\\,$ | $\\,0.9998\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 4)=P(X>3).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =P(X>3) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-F(3) \\\\  & =1-0.8571 \\\\  & =0.1429.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166737 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e597d4c-f86f-509e-9fc8-7dd7c03125a1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d179069-c017-58b3-9681-83c19b40173a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3498" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487626} {:answer/id #uuid "309d8cdc-a45a-5ab5-9a3b-49832ed6d041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7405" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487659} {:answer/id #uuid "4e5423c0-285d-57a6-9979-2880e8d5ce6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487721} {:answer/id #uuid "d0965698-05e5-51b1-b407-9a7f58296fee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3837" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487965} {:answer/id #uuid "df40732a-9e2e-5e0c-bf2d-69ad5340e4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5154" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df40732a-9e2e-5e0c-bf2d-69ad5340e4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5154" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487992} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb9b6fe0-9e0e-55d1-807b-86e15edd4fae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f97c8702-16dc-518f-875a-9b5c78750b8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-224965" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(4)$ given below, compute $P(3<X\\le 7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.2381\\,$ | $\\,0.4335\\,$ | $\\,0.6288\\,$ | $\\,0.7851\\,$ | $\\,0.8893\\,$ | $\\,0.9489\\,$ | $\\,0.9786\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\})+P(X\\in \\{4,5,6,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3)+P(3<X\\le 7) \\\\  & =F(3)+P(3<X\\le 7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X\\le 7) & =F(7)-F(3) \\\\  & =0.9489-0.4335 \\\\  & =0.5154.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488276 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "387be734-719f-52cd-8079-50c744ecdd5e" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Poisson CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13ae6705-d6fa-5a1b-a345-6039c632303a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0174" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13ae6705-d6fa-5a1b-a345-6039c632303a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0174" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487609} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b8adfb2-b2e2-5e9c-ae22-d60ba87a03a5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488067} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b6d52ea-41c1-5b97-a72e-2af5e66233c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0025" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b6d52ea-41c1-5b97-a72e-2af5e66233c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0025" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487858} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2715bda-0578-54f8-a6f8-d5f30a7d8e25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488149}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7faa58d-c8b1-553c-876f-43b3b6090485" :question/math-academy-id "q-224984" :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(6).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing values in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.0620\\,$ | $\\,0.1512\\,$ | $\\,0.2851\\,$ | $\\,0.4457\\,$ | $\\,0.6063\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =6.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{0}{e}^{-6}}{0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0025\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{0}\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{0!}+\\frac{{6}^{1}\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1}+\\frac{6\\cdot {e}^{-6}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0174\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "387be734-719f-52cd-8079-50c744ecdd5e" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Poisson CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cf46e97-2c49-5dc4-9720-738d9fcbf422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0009" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cf46e97-2c49-5dc4-9720-738d9fcbf422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0009" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487683} :answer-field/id #uuid "04f5f413-0f98-5505-983e-d59a63258e11" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1424711-bfed-5b96-95b9-807b329960d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0073" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1424711-bfed-5b96-95b9-807b329960d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0073" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487966} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c72a0ab-81d8-5720-a0ce-49a7974bca0d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fef70086-7b53-5958-83a3-40bb6490de70" :question/math-academy-id "q-224988" :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(7).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing values in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.0296\\,$ | $\\,0.0818\\,$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =7.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{7}^{0}{e}^{-7}}{0!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0009\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{7}^{0}\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{0!}+\\frac{{7}^{1}\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1}+\\frac{7\\cdot {e}^{-7}}{1} \\\\  & ≈0.0073\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "387be734-719f-52cd-8079-50c744ecdd5e" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Poisson CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5542ee15-2183-5eb0-9267-aae1b75ac496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1550" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5542ee15-2183-5eb0-9267-aae1b75ac496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1550" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487736} :answer-field/id #uuid "76d83c0e-8572-5ffe-a152-9df51921452d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488100}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "06c6c230-3fa4-5b71-a2c3-1d7beda8e3c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-224989" :question/problem "Consider the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(12).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal digits, fill in the missing value in the corresponding table for the cumulative distribution function below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0203\\,$ | $\\,0.0458\\,$ | $\\,0.0895\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $\\,0.2424\\,$ | $\\,0.3472\\,$ | $\\,0.4616\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Poisson distribution $\\text{Po}(\\lambda )$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,3,…\\,.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda =12.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8) & =P(X\\le 8) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 7)+P(X=8) \\\\  & =F(7)+P(X=8) \\\\  & =0.0895+\\frac{{12}^{8}\\cdot {e}^{-12}}{8!} \\\\  & ≈0.1550\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166736 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "240ed915-56cd-5e22-8c7f-a36ebea90279" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Using a CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5829e646-b58a-5440-a9ba-2533382195ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3472" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5829e646-b58a-5440-a9ba-2533382195ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3472" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487744} :answer-field/id #uuid "93c362b2-2bb8-51e2-be3b-426a0b40223d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77a09fd4-a75e-503e-85e7-5369cc0e38f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-224998" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(12)$ given below, compute $P(X<11).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $13$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0895\\,$ | $\\,0.1550\\,$ | $\\,0.2424\\,$ | $\\,0.3472\\,$ | $\\,0.4616\\,$ | $\\,0.5760\\,$ | $\\,0.6815\\,$ |\n\n$P(X<11)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<11) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,10\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 10) \\\\  & =F(10) \\\\  & =0.3472.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166736 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "240ed915-56cd-5e22-8c7f-a36ebea90279" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Using a CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bb640e7-0a11-5457-b2f5-9e615281af0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7622" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bb640e7-0a11-5457-b2f5-9e615281af0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7622" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487832} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b252531-9953-5c30-bea3-fc9fef82d0df" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47d084d0-558c-55b5-8190-75e291aec240" :question/math-academy-id "q-224999" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5)$ given below, compute $P(X<7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.2650\\,$ | $\\,0.4405\\,$ | $\\,0.6160\\,$ | $\\,0.7622\\,$ | $\\,0.8666\\,$ | $\\,0.9319\\,$ | $\\,0.9682\\,$ |\n\n$P(X<7)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<7) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(6) \\\\  & =0.7622.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166736 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "240ed915-56cd-5e22-8c7f-a36ebea90279" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Using a CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fba073e2-4b1f-5dc6-b5ca-445184ad40a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0901" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fba073e2-4b1f-5dc6-b5ca-445184ad40a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0901" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488039} :answer-field/id #uuid "051c70a8-cf85-5100-9515-597f30cc3693" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6ed46a6a-33c2-5d2f-895f-2046417a88d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-225004" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(10)$ given below, compute $P(X=7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0103\\,$ | $\\,0.0293\\,$ | $\\,0.0671\\,$ | $\\,0.1301\\,$ | $\\,0.2202\\,$ | $\\,0.3328\\,$ | $\\,0.4579\\,$ |\n\n$P(X=7)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\})+P(X=7) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6)+P(X=7) \\\\  & =F(6)+P(X=7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=7) & =F(7)-F(6) \\\\  & =0.2202-0.1301 \\\\  & =0.0901.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488266 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166737 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e597d4c-f86f-509e-9fc8-7dd7c03125a1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5511111d-5afd-5b22-bb89-1ea91a4838c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7655" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487735} {:answer/id #uuid "568f563b-3443-50b8-bb56-4f2da7c0db5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8153" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487738} {:answer/id #uuid "c293f896-5431-56fb-8b53-6b9eaa071c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7170" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487935} {:answer/id #uuid "ca8aa39f-446f-5831-af5e-ebb6ebecaa92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6162" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487953} {:answer/id #uuid "f589b1b7-5f83-5709-a135-a5673ac3bb61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8663" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5511111d-5afd-5b22-bb89-1ea91a4838c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7655" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487735} :answer-field/id #uuid "de4d3525-6787-5129-8466-0e3b6a451cdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0dd1d6e-e305-5637-930e-c61c5f8b750e" :question/math-academy-id "q-225056" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(3)$ given below, compute $P(1\\le X\\le 4).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0498\\,$ | $\\,0.1991\\,$ | $\\,0.4232\\,$ | $\\,0.6472\\,$ | $\\,0.8153\\,$ | $\\,0.9161\\,$ | $\\,0.9665\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0\\})+P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0)+P(1\\le X\\le 4) \\\\  & =F(0)+P(1\\le X\\le 4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X\\le 4) & =F(4)-F(0) \\\\  & =0.8153-0.0498 \\\\  & =0.7655.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166737 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e597d4c-f86f-509e-9fc8-7dd7c03125a1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c475843-a998-5eb6-bedd-a6c61b6df4af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6298" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487752} {:answer/id #uuid "6767ed18-37b4-52b6-b3b4-2902bf4479f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7486" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487775} {:answer/id #uuid "a56f7c2f-fa79-56b2-bce2-b9c0448e7be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5610" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487875} {:answer/id #uuid "aa628303-b89a-5a92-ae53-de779c29dcce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7916" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487894} {:answer/id #uuid "f6cb2bc3-6add-5539-b50b-575b65928967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6798" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c475843-a998-5eb6-bedd-a6c61b6df4af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6298" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487752} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce36e3da-c7d4-5674-90dc-86313309fe07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9431e7c-b663-534c-b1f2-e2cde30992c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-225057" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(6.5)$ given below, compute $P(3\\le X\\le 7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0430\\,$ | $\\,0.1118\\,$ | $\\,0.2237\\,$ | $\\,0.3690\\,$ | $\\,0.5265\\,$ | $\\,0.6728\\,$ | $\\,0.7916\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5,6,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(3\\le X\\le 7) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(3\\le X\\le 7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 7) & =F(7)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.6728-0.0430 \\\\  & =0.6298.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166737 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e597d4c-f86f-509e-9fc8-7dd7c03125a1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ae0e9c0-dec1-57ea-83c6-26d6b6f4215e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6247" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487679} {:answer/id #uuid "4d3e08c2-6ab6-554b-a95c-c2795a89a993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8159" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487718} {:answer/id #uuid "5859446f-1105-516b-a9db-47ed0b0b6da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6170" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487745} {:answer/id #uuid "6928677a-241c-5b13-8914-64885e8b9340" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7163" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487776} {:answer/id #uuid "c7c8c73d-7ec6-551e-abb6-3d12a4c29a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4013" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7c8c73d-7ec6-551e-abb6-3d12a4c29a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4013" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487947} :answer-field/id #uuid "67c0c25f-5114-5911-a607-39d35b3593d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bfd17aa5-30fb-5cb9-aef8-99d3d322cf8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-225061" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(5<X<9).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ | $\\,0.7166\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8) & =P(X<9) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,8\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\})+P(X\\in \\{6,7,8\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 5)+P(5<X<9) \\\\  & =F(5)+P(5<X<9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5<X<9) & =F(8)-F(5) \\\\  & =0.5925-0.1912 \\\\  & =0.4013.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166737 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e597d4c-f86f-509e-9fc8-7dd7c03125a1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Poisson Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87766c55-68f3-5682-b6fb-94ccde26296e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6594" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87766c55-68f3-5682-b6fb-94ccde26296e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6594" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487823} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd524d5-d969-5fdc-85e1-96731361041c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3fd62c03-4c13-5eaa-a871-a2d0ae21b2c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-225064" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5.5)$ given below, compute $P(1<X<7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0266\\,$ | $\\,0.0884\\,$ | $\\,0.2017\\,$ | $\\,0.3575\\,$ | $\\,0.5289\\,$ | $\\,0.6860\\,$ | $\\,0.8095\\,$ |\n\n$P(1<X<7)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X<7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1\\})+P(X\\in \\{2,3,4,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(1<X<7) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(1<X<7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<7) & =F(6)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.6860-0.0266 \\\\  & =0.6594.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166738 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e822ac5d-67a0-57b5-b5fe-d3ad03cd91fe" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Containing a \"Greater Than\" Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f01f279-b478-5b3b-9f12-398739dfd7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0839" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487655} {:answer/id #uuid "49ec3dad-10b2-586c-9514-ba768dab6a50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8153" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487711} {:answer/id #uuid "4e48dc12-e75f-5206-a9ab-cb83f164828a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0335" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487720} {:answer/id #uuid "8f5bcdba-d33b-591c-8f35-7033f93c02d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1847" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487840} {:answer/id #uuid "f9582ec0-20d1-5343-8